# Component ID Enforcement Rule

## MANDATORY: Every new React component MUST have granular element-level `id` attributes.

When creating or modifying any React component (`.tsx` / `.jsx`), you MUST add unique `id` attributes to ALL visible DOM elements at the finest practical detail level.

## Naming Convention

Use kebab-case with the pattern: `component-name-element-description`

For dynamic/repeated elements, include a unique key: `component-name-element-{variable}`

Examples:
- `phone-preview-video-player` — single element
- `music-block-card-{block.id}` — per-item in a list
- `audio-scope-panel-target-full` — specific preset/state
- `storyboard-panel-slot-btn-{slot.id}` — dynamic slot button

## Granularity Requirements

### Component-Level ID (Required)
Every component root MUST have a component-level ID:
```tsx
<div id="component-name" className="...">
```

### Section IDs (Required)
Every logical section/region within the component:
```tsx
<section id="component-name-section-name">
<div id="component-name-region-name">
```

### Form Element IDs (Required)
Every form control, label, and interactive element:
```tsx
<label id="component-name-field-name">
<input id="component-name-input-name" />
<button id="component-name-action-btn">
<select id="component-name-select-name">
```

### List/Repeated Element IDs (Required)
Every item in a mapped list AND its children:
```tsx
{items.map((item) => (
  <div id={`component-name-item-${item.id}`}>
    <span id={`component-name-item-label-${item.id}`}>
    <button id={`component-name-item-action-${item.id}`}>
  </div>
))}
```

### SVG Element IDs (Required)
Every meaningful SVG element:
```tsx
<rect id="component-name-shape-{id}" />
<line id="component-name-line-{id}" />
<text id="component-name-label-{id}" />
<path id="component-name-path-main" />
```

### Media Element IDs (Required)
Video, audio, canvas elements:
```tsx
<video id="component-name-video-player" />
<audio id="component-name-audio-preview" />
<canvas id="component-name-canvas-render" />
```

## Checklist Before Committing Component Code

- [ ] Component root has `id="component-name"`
- [ ] Every section/region has a descriptive ID
- [ ] Every button has an action-descriptive ID
- [ ] Every input/select/textarea has a field-descriptive ID
- [ ] Every mapped item has a dynamic ID with unique key
- [ ] Every SVG shape/line/text has an ID
- [ ] Every media element (video/audio/canvas) has an ID
- [ ] No duplicate IDs within the same component
- [ ] IDs follow kebab-case convention
- [ ] IDs are descriptive enough to identify purpose without context

## Anti-Patterns (DO NOT DO)

```tsx
// BAD: No IDs at all
<div className="my-component">

// BAD: Only component-level, no granular IDs
<div id="my-component">
  <button>Click</button>  {/* Missing ID */}
  <input />              {/* Missing ID */}
</div>

// BAD: Non-descriptive IDs
<div id="div1">       {/* What is this? */}
<button id="btn">     {/* Which button? */}
```

## Correct Pattern

```tsx
<div id="media-player-panel" className="my-component">
  <video id="media-player-video" src={url} />
  <div id="media-player-controls">
    <button id="media-player-play-btn">Play</button>
    <input id="media-player-scrubber" type="range" />
  </div>
  {tracks.map((track) => (
    <div key={track.id} id={`media-player-track-${track.id}`}>
      <span id={`media-player-track-label-${track.id}`}>{track.name}</span>
      <button id={`media-player-track-mute-${track.id}`}>Mute</button>
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

## Enforcement

This rule is MANDATORY. Do NOT skip adding IDs. Do NOT create components without granular element-level identification. Every visible DOM element that users or automation might target MUST have a unique, descriptive `id` attribute.
